---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data: calculations run in your browser, we keep no record of your figures, and the page address carries your inputs so results can be shared.`}
  updated="2026-10-17"
  legal
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a salary calculator. The short version of this policy:{' '}
    <strong>your salary is calculated in your browser, and we keep no record of it.</strong> There
    are no accounts, no sign-up and no database of salary details.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens to the figures you enter</h2>
  <p>
    Every calculation runs as JavaScript inside your browser. Your CTC, allowances, rent, deductions
    and the results are not sent to us as data. They do appear in the page address, as the next
    sections explain.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    To save you retyping, the calculator keeps your most recent inputs, your advanced-mode settings
    and your light or dark theme choice in your browser's <strong>local storage</strong>. This data
    stays on your device, is never sent to us, and is deleted when you clear your browser's site
    data. You can also use the calculator's reset button to clear it.
  </p>

  <h2>The page address contains your inputs</h2>
  <p>
    As you type, the calculator keeps your inputs in the page address (the part after the{' '}
    <code>?</code>), so a result can be bookmarked, reloaded or shared and still show the same
    figures. That has two consequences:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      When you reload the page or open such a link, your browser requests that address from our host
      like any other, so the figures in it reach the host's servers and may appear in its request
      logs. We do not collect or analyse them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Anyone you send the link to, and any service that sees it along the way (a chat app or email
      provider, for example), can read the salary figures in it. Share links only with people you
      are comfortable showing those numbers to.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Exports</h2>
  <p>
    PDF and Excel files are generated in your browser and saved straight to your device. They are
    not uploaded anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical
    request data such as IP addresses and browser type in order to deliver pages and protect against
    abuse. It includes the page address requested, which carries your calculator inputs when you
    reload the calculator or open a share link. See{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">
      Cloudflare's privacy policy
    </a>{' '}
    for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Visit statistics and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    To see how many people use the site and which pages help them, {SITE.name} uses{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">
      Cloudflare Web Analytics
    </a>
    . A small script from Cloudflare reports each page view: the page path, the site you came from,
    your country, browser, operating system and device type, and how quickly the page loaded. We see
    only totals, such as page views per day.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare states that Web Analytics uses no cookies or local storage, does not track individual
    visitors across websites, and{' '}
    <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/faq/" rel="noopener">
      does not log query strings
    </a>
    , so the salary figures in the page address are not part of these statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site sets no advertising cookies and uses no tracking pixels. Fonts and icons are served
    from this site, not from third-party font services.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We may show advertisements through Google AdSense in future to keep the calculator free. If we
    do, this section will be updated before ads go live. In that case:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google and its partners use cookies to serve ads based on your visits to this and other
      websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising at{' '}
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>
      , and learn more at{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">
        How Google uses cookies in advertising
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>Advertisers never receive the figures you enter into the calculator.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The calculator is intended for working adults and is not directed at children. We do not
    knowingly collect information from anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not collect personal data about you (the visit statistics above are anonymous
    totals), there is nothing held by us to access, correct or delete. Data stored in your browser
    is under your control and can be removed at any time by clearing site data.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with an updated date at the
    top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
